{"resourceIdentifier":"411","resourceName":"Chorchaiwat Wastewater Treatment and Biogas Utilization Project","description":"The wastewater treatment plant was implemented at Chorchaiwat Industry Co., Ltd. in 2005. The starch plant has a total production capacity of 200 tonnes of native starch per day, generating up to 3,000 m3 of wastewater every production day at the maximum capacity of the plant. The project has been in operation since June 20071. Prior to implementation of the project activity, the wastewater of the starch plant was treated in 6 cascading open anaerobic lagoons, with a retention time of more than 160 days. The minimum depth of these ponds is 5m from the water surface. The average atmospheric temperature in the region is 28 degrees Celsius2. These conditions result in anaerobic environment within the ponds, resulting in methane generation from the organic content (characterized by chemical oxygen demand or COD) of the wastewater.","location":{"latitude":12.838880,"longitude":100.957139},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"411"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Chonburi Province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Chorchaiwat Industry Co., Ltd."},{"type":"string","value":"Wattana, Thailand"},{"type":"string","value":"+66 38 239 120"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"411"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"26662"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AMS-I.C.,AMS-III.H."}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"KBS Certification Services Limited"}]},{"